; react-simple-maps@3 still lists its React peer as 16/17/18 (no React 19 yet)
; but runs fine on the React 19 we use. This keeps installs resolving without
; --legacy-peer-deps on every command. NOTE: it's global, so it also silences
; any other peer conflicts — re-check on major dep bumps. Remove once
; react-simple-maps ships a release that lists react@19 in peerDependencies.
legacy-peer-deps=true
